{"format":"vetro-plugin","version":1,"manifest":{"id":"ambilight","name":"Ambilight","version":"1.0.0","apiVersion":1,"permissions":["exec"],"author":"local","description":"Starts the USB ambilight service on boot and controls it from the dashboard.","main":"index.js","ui":{"label":"Ambilight"}},"files":{"README.md":"# Ambilight Shard\n\nStarts the USB ambilight service (`/opt/ambilight/AmbilightUsb.dll`) when the TV boots, and gives\nthe dashboard a Start / Stop / Restart button plus the tail of `run.log`.\n\n## Why a Shard\n\n`/etc` is read-only on this firmware, the capture libraries only work from a root process outside the\nTizen app sandbox, and the service cannot be a TPK. A Vetro Shard is the only mechanism on this TV\nthat already survives a reboot (`ctx.execute` runs as root, the same way the SSH server does).\n\n## Install (by hand, over SSH)\n\n```sh\nP=/opt/usr/home/owner/share/vetro-plugins\nmkdir -p $P/ambilight\n# copy manifest.json, index.js and ui.html into $P/ambilight/\nchown -R owner:users $P/ambilight\n```\n\nThen open **Vetro Shards** in the dashboard: the folder appears as *Ambilight* (source: copied in by\nhand) and must be **switched on** — a Shard never runs until it is enabled. If the build refuses\nunsigned Shards, turn on **Developer mode** first (Plugins → Add a plugin).\n\nSwitching it on runs `start()` immediately and at every boot afterwards.\n\n## What it runs\n\n`start`:\n\n```sh\nmodprobe cdc_acm                        # not persistent across a reboot\nsetsid nohup /usr/bin/dotnet /opt/ambilight/AmbilightUsb.dll \\\n    >> /opt/ambilight/run.log 2>&1 < /dev/null &\n```\n\n`stop` touches `/tmp/ambilight.stop`. The service polls that file at the top of its render loop and\nshuts down on its own thread — it is **never** SIGKILLed, because tearing it down while it is inside\n`secvideo_api_capture_video_main` wedges the TV's scaler until the set is power-cycled.\n\n## Files the service needs on the TV\n\n| path | |\n|---|---|\n| `/opt/ambilight/AmbilightUsb.dll` | the app (+ `.deps.json`, `.runtimeconfig.json`) |\n| `/opt/usr/share/ambilight/config.json` | settings, see the fork's README |\n\n## Settings tab\n\nThe Shard's tab has a **Settings** section on top of Start / Stop / Restart and the log tail:\n\n| group | fields |\n|---|---|\n| Geometry | LED count, zone count, **exact per-edge cut counts (top/right/bottom/left)**, start offset, reverse, edge band fraction, letterbox crop and threshold |\n| Look & feel | smoothing (alpha), gamma, saturation, black level, neighbour blur, HDR peak nits, HDR/PQ input and BT.2020→BT.709 gamut mapping, target fps, still-image fade delay/level, scene punch |\n\n- **Ambilight: ON/OFF** is a live output switch: it writes `enable=0/1` to `/tmp/amb-control` (the\n  app's local control file when no `controlUrl` is set) and persists `outputEnabled` in config. The\n  service keeps running; with output off no frames are sent and the SCORPIO blanks the strip after\n  ~400 ms. Turning it back on resumes immediately.\n- **Save** writes `/opt/usr/share/ambilight/config.json`; **Save & restart** also stops the service via\n  the stop file and starts it again, because the app reads its config only at startup.\n- A **layout preview** draws the 16:9 TV outline with all zone positions and the LEDs coloured in\n  physical order (red→green→blue). It uses the same perimeter distribution and walk order as\n  `ZoneEngine.cs`, so what you see is the order the strip actually receives. Click/drag the ring to\n  place LED 0 (sets `mapOffset`); **Flip direction** toggles `mapReverse`; **Start top-left** and\n  **My cut** are useful presets. On this TV the strip is one continuous 300-LED ring with no bottom\n  gap: cut 97/53/97/53, starting at the bottom-right corner and running counter-clockwise\n  (`mapOffset=149`, `mapReverse=1`).\n- On load the panel probes the board with the hello frame and reads `AMBI1 <count> <type>` from its\n  banner. LED count, zone count and the offset are clamped to that compiled-in value — an oversized\n  config would silently drop every frame. When the service is running the port cannot be probed, so the\n  last successful answer (kept in the Shard's own `config.json`) is used and labelled `cached`.\n- Presets: **77″ / 300 LEDs** restores the values this TV is calibrated with (the same numbers in both\n  `DEFAULTS` objects, including `hdr=0` / `gamut=0` for SDR); **Reset geometry** clears the\n  offset/direction/crop settings without touching the look & feel values.\n- Only the fields above are written; `serialDevice` (the stable `/dev/serial/by-id` symlink), the\n  backend and all other keys are preserved untouched.\n\n**Why file access goes through `ctx.execute`:** the Vetro process can read files inside its own plugin\nfolder but gets EACCES on `/opt/usr/share/...` and `/opt/ambilight/run.log` (Tizen/Smack). The Shard\nreads and writes the app config and tails the log with root shell commands; only `ui.html` is read\nwith `fs`, because that lives in the Shard's own folder.\n\n## Status fields\n\n| field | meaning |\n|---|---|\n| `state` | `running` / `stopped` |\n| `device` | whether `/dev/ttyACM1` exists (the SCORPIO) |\n| `module` | whether `cdc_acm` is loaded |\n| `serial` | last \"serial port open\" line (confirms the port was opened) |\n| `capture` | last capture problem, if any (`rc=-2` = wedged scaler, needs a reboot) |\n","index.js":"'use strict';\n// Ambilight Shard: starts the USB ambilight service when the TV boots and gives the dashboard a\n// start/stop/log view of it.\n//\n// WHY A PLUGIN AT ALL: /etc is read-only on this firmware and the capture libraries only work from\n// a root process outside the Tizen app sandbox, so the service cannot be a TPK and cannot be a\n// systemd unit. A Vetro Shard is the mechanism that already survives a reboot on this TV (the SSH\n// server is one), and `ctx.execute` runs as root.\n//\n// Two things are deliberate:\n//   * The service is started DETACHED (`setsid nohup ... &` with all three descriptors redirected).\n//     ctx.execute has a 60 s cap and a shared command queue, so a foreground child would either be\n//     killed or block every other Shard.\n//   * Stop uses a stop FILE, never SIGKILL. The render loop is routinely inside a blocking native\n//     capture call; tearing the process down there wedges the TV's scaler until the set is power\n//     cycled (measured, 4 times). The app polls /tmp/ambilight.stop and shuts itself down on the\n//     only thread allowed to leave that call.\nvar fs = require('fs');\nvar path = require('path');\n\nvar APP = '/opt/ambilight/AmbilightUsb.dll';\nvar LOG = '/opt/ambilight/run.log';\nvar STOPFILE = '/tmp/ambilight.stop';\n// The check MUST be anchored to the start of the command line. An unanchored literal matched the\n// `sh -c` wrapper that is itself running this script (its arguments contain the same string), so\n// start() always reported \"already running\" and launched nothing; a bracket-escaped regex matched\n// nothing at all on this TV's busybox. The anchored form matches only the real dotnet process.\nvar MATCH = '^/usr/bin/dotnet /opt/ambilight/AmbilightUsb.dll';\nvar CONFIG = '/opt/usr/share/ambilight/config.json';\n\n// Fields the settings tab may change, with the same clamps the C# config reader applies. Geometry is\n// the part that decides WHERE light goes; the rest decides HOW it looks. Everything else in config.json\n// (serialDevice, backend, ...) is preserved untouched on save.\nvar SPECS = {\n    outputEnabled: ['int', 0, 1],\n    ledCount:   ['int', 1, 2048],\n    zoneCount:  ['int', 1, 2048],\n    zoneTop:    ['int', 0, 2048],\n    zoneRight:  ['int', 0, 2048],\n    zoneBottom: ['int', 0, 2048],\n    zoneLeft:   ['int', 0, 2048],\n    mapOffset:  ['int', 0, 2047],\n    mapReverse: ['int', 0, 1],\n    bandFrac:   ['num', 0.01, 0.50],\n    bars:       ['int', 0, 1],\n    barRows:    ['int', 0, 1],\n    barThresh:  ['int', 0, 255],\n    alpha:      ['num', 0, 1],\n    gamma:      ['num', 0.5, 4],\n    adaptiveGamma: ['num', 0, 1],\n    saturation: ['num', 0.5, 1],\n    black:      ['num', 0, 200],\n    spatial:    ['num', 0, 1],\n    peak:       ['num', 100, 4000],\n    hdr:        ['int', 0, 1],\n    gamut:      ['int', 0, 1],\n    targetFps:  ['int', 0, 120],\n    staleMs:    ['num', 0, 60000],\n    staleLevel: ['num', 0, 1],\n    punch:      ['num', 0, 1]\n};\n\n// The \"77 inch / 300 LED\" preset: the values this TV is calibrated with. Kept in sync with the\n// ui.html DEFAULTS and with the working /opt/usr/share/ambilight/config.json. hdr/gamut=0 are\n// required for SDR content - the PQ/BT.2020 path shifts saturated hues (orange -> yellow).\nvar DEFAULTS = {\n    outputEnabled: 1,\n    ledCount: 300, zoneCount: 300, zoneTop: 97, zoneRight: 53, zoneBottom: 97, zoneLeft: 53,\n    mapOffset: 149, mapReverse: 1, bandFrac: 0.08,\n    // saturation stays 1: >1 expands chroma BEFORE the BT.601 matrix, which drives low channels\n    // negative and clips them to zero (a warm green lost all its red - measured on the TV).\n    bars: 1, barRows: 0, barThresh: 18, alpha: 0.25, gamma: 1, saturation: 1, adaptiveGamma: 0,\n    black: 2, spatial: 0.15, peak: 400, hdr: 0, gamut: 0,\n    targetFps: 25, staleMs: 6000, staleLevel: 0.35, punch: 0\n};\n\nvar START = [\n    'export DOTNET_SYSTEM_GLOBALIZATION_INVARIANT=1',\n    // modprobe is not persistent across a reboot and the CDC device node only exists once the\n    // module is loaded.\n    'if ! lsmod | grep -q \"^cdc_acm\"; then modprobe cdc_acm 2>/dev/null; fi',\n    'rm -f ' + STOPFILE,\n    'if pgrep -f \"' + MATCH + '\" >/dev/null; then echo \"already running\"; exit 0; fi',\n    'if [ ! -f ' + APP + ' ]; then echo \"missing ' + APP + '\"; exit 3; fi',\n    'mkdir -p /opt/usr/share/ambilight /opt/ambilight',\n    'setsid nohup /usr/bin/dotnet ' + APP + ' >> ' + LOG + ' 2>&1 < /dev/null &',\n    'sleep 3',\n    'if pgrep -f \"' + MATCH + '\" >/dev/null; then echo \"started\"; else echo \"FAILED to start\"; tail -n 5 ' + LOG + '; exit 4; fi'\n].join('\\n');\n\nvar STOP = [\n    'if ! pgrep -f \"' + MATCH + '\" >/dev/null; then echo \"not running\"; exit 0; fi',\n    'touch ' + STOPFILE,\n    'i=0; while [ $i -lt 25 ] && pgrep -f \"' + MATCH + '\" >/dev/null; do i=$((i+1)); sleep 1; done',\n    'if pgrep -f \"' + MATCH + '\" >/dev/null; then echo \"STILL RUNNING after 25 s - left alone on purpose\"; exit 5; fi',\n    'echo \"stopped\"'\n].join('\\n');\n\nvar STATE = [\n    'P=$(pgrep -f \"' + MATCH + '\" | head -n 1)',\n    'if [ -n \"$P\" ]; then echo \"state=running pid=$P\"; else echo \"state=stopped\"; fi',\n    'D=$(sed -n \"s/.*\\\\\\\"serialDevice\\\\\\\"[[:space:]]*:[[:space:]]*\\\\\\\"\\\\([^\\\\\\\"]*\\\\)\\\\\\\".*/\\\\1/p\" ' + CONFIG + ')',\n    'if [ -z \"$D\" ]; then D=/dev/ttyACM1; fi',\n    'if [ -e \"$D\" ]; then echo \"device=$D present\"; else echo \"device=$D MISSING\"; fi',\n    'if lsmod | grep -q \"^cdc_acm\"; then echo \"module=cdc_acm loaded\"; else echo \"module=cdc_acm NOT loaded\"; fi',\n    'grep \"=== \" ' + LOG + ' 2>/dev/null | tail -n 1 | sed \"s/^/version=/\"',\n    'grep \"serial port open\" ' + LOG + ' 2>/dev/null | tail -n 1 | sed \"s/^/serial=/\"',\n    'grep \"no video-plane frame\" ' + LOG + ' 2>/dev/null | tail -n 1 | sed \"s/^/capture_problem=/\"'\n].join('\\n');\n\nfunction readConfigAsync(ctx, cb) {\n    // The Vetro process can read its own plugin folder but NOT /opt/usr/share/... directly (Smack:\n    // fs.readFileSync returns EACCES there). ctx.execute runs as root and is the only way through.\n    var p = run(ctx, 'cat ' + CONFIG + ' 2>/dev/null', 5000);\n    if (!p) { cb({}); return; }\n    p.then(function (r) {\n        try {\n            var c = JSON.parse(String((r && r.stdout) || ''));\n            cb(c && typeof c === 'object' ? c : {});\n        } catch (e) { cb({}); }\n    }, function () { cb({}); });\n}\n\n// Returns { clean: {...}, errors: [...] }. Never writes anything itself. `fwLeds` comes from the\n// firmware banner, so a config larger than the compiled strip can never be saved from the UI.\nfunction validate(values, fwLeds) {\n    var clean = {}, errors = [];\n    if (!values || typeof values !== 'object') return { clean: clean, errors: ['no values supplied'] };\n    for (var key in SPECS) {\n        if (!Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(values, key)) continue;\n        var spec = SPECS[key], v = values[key];\n        if (spec[0] === 'int') v = Math.floor(Number(v));\n        else v = Number(v);\n        if (!isFinite(v)) { errors.push(key + ': not a number'); continue; }\n        var hi = spec[2];\n        if (key === 'ledCount' && fwLeds > 0) hi = Math.min(hi, fwLeds);\n        if (key === 'zoneCount') hi = Math.min(hi, Number(clean.ledCount || values.ledCount || 2048));\n        if (v < spec[1] || v > hi) { errors.push(key + ': must be ' + spec[1] + '..' + hi); continue; }\n        clean[key] = v;\n    }\n    return { clean: clean, errors: errors };\n}\n\nfunction run(ctx, cmd, ms) {\n    try { return ctx.execute(cmd, ms || 20000); }\n    catch (e) { return null; }\n}\n\nmodule.exports = function (ctx) {\n    var cache = { state: 'unknown', log: [], lastAction: null, lastError: null };\n\n    function remember(text) {\n        var lines = String(text || '').split('\\n');\n        var out = { log: [] };\n        for (var i = 0; i < lines.length; i++) {\n            var l = lines[i];\n            if (/^state=/.test(l)) out.state = l.slice(6);\n            else if (/^pid=/.test(l)) out.pid = l.slice(4);\n            else if (/^device=/.test(l)) out.device = l.slice(7);\n            else if (/^module=/.test(l)) out.module = l.slice(7);\n            else if (/^version=/.test(l)) out.version = l.slice(8);\n            else if (/^serial=/.test(l)) out.serial = l.slice(7);\n            else if (/^capture_problem=/.test(l)) out.captureProblem = l.slice(16);\n            else if (l.length) out.log.push(l);\n        }\n        return out;\n    }\n\n    function refresh(cb) {\n        var p = run(ctx, STATE, 12000);\n        if (!p) { if (cb) cb(); return; }\n        p.then(function (r) {\n            var s = remember((r && r.stdout) || '');\n            if (s.state) cache.state = s.state;\n            if (s.device) cache.device = s.device;\n            if (s.module) cache.module = s.module;\n            if (s.version) cache.version = s.version;\n            if (s.serial) cache.serial = s.serial;\n            if (s.captureProblem) cache.captureProblem = s.captureProblem;\n            if (s.pid) cache.pid = s.pid;\n            if (cb) cb();\n        }, function (e) { cache.lastError = String(e && e.message || e); if (cb) cb(); });\n    }\n\n    // At boot Vetro starts Shards before its root helper is connected. ctx.execute then rejects with\n    // \"no root agent connected\" and the service would never start until someone re-enabled the Shard\n    // (measured after a reboot: Shard running, lastAction = start -> error: no root agent connected).\n    // Retry that specific condition for up to ~110 s; any other error is reported at once, because\n    // retrying a broken command would only spam the shared execute queue.\n    var RETRY_DELAYS = [5000, 15000, 30000, 60000, 60000];\n\n    function failed(name, msg, cb) {\n        cache.lastError = msg;\n        cache.lastAction = name + ' -> error: ' + msg;\n        if (cb) cb(null);\n    }\n\n    function attempt(cmd, ms, name, idx, cb) {\n        var p = run(ctx, cmd, ms);\n        if (!p) {\n            if (idx < RETRY_DELAYS.length) {\n                cache.lastAction = name + ' -> no root agent, retry ' + (idx + 1) + ' in ' +\n                                   (RETRY_DELAYS[idx] / 1000) + 's';\n                setTimeout(function () { attempt(cmd, ms, name, idx + 1, cb); }, RETRY_DELAYS[idx]);\n                return;\n            }\n            failed(name, 'execute unavailable', cb);\n            return;\n        }\n        p.then(function (r) {\n            cache.lastAction = name + ' -> ' + String((r && r.stdout) || '').trim();\n            cache.lastError = null;\n            refresh(function () { if (cb) cb(r); });\n        }, function (e) {\n            var msg = String(e && e.message || e);\n            if (idx < RETRY_DELAYS.length && /root agent|not connected|no agent/i.test(msg)) {\n                cache.lastAction = name + ' -> waiting for root agent, retry ' + (idx + 1) + ' in ' +\n                                   (RETRY_DELAYS[idx] / 1000) + 's';\n                setTimeout(function () { attempt(cmd, ms, name, idx + 1, cb); }, RETRY_DELAYS[idx]);\n                return;\n            }\n            failed(name, msg, cb);\n        });\n    }\n\n    function act(cmd, ms, name, cb) {\n        attempt(cmd, ms, name, 0, cb);\n    }\n\n    function json(res, body, code) {\n        res.writeHead(code || 200, { 'content-type': 'application/json', 'cache-control': 'no-store' });\n        res.end(JSON.stringify(body));\n    }\n\n    function logTail(n, cb) {\n        var p = run(ctx, 'tail -n ' + (n || 40) + ' ' + LOG + ' 2>/dev/null', 5000);\n        if (!p) { cb('(no log yet)'); return; }\n        p.then(function (r) { cb(String((r && r.stdout) || '(no log yet)')); },\n               function () { cb('(no log yet)'); });\n    }\n\n    function loadPage() {\n        var places = [path.join(__dirname, 'ui.html'), path.join(ctx.dir || '', 'ui.html')];\n        for (var i = 0; i < places.length; i++) {\n            try { return fs.readFileSync(places[i], 'utf8'); } catch (e) {}\n        }\n        return '<!doctype html><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><p>ui.html missing: reinstall this Shard.</p>';\n    }\n\n    // Ask the board itself how many LEDs it was compiled for: a config larger than that silently drops\n    // frames. Probing needs the port, so it is only done while the service is stopped; otherwise use the\n    // last successful answer kept in the Shard's own config.json.\n    function probeFirmware(cb) {\n        var saved = ctx.config.get() || {};\n        var cached = {\n            leds: Number(saved.firmwareLeds) || 300,\n            type: saved.firmwareType || 'RGBW',\n            source: 'cached'\n        };\n        readConfigAsync(ctx, function (cfg) {\n            probeWithDevice(cfg.serialDevice, cached, cb);\n        });\n    }\n\n    function probeWithDevice(device, cached, cb) {\n        var dev = String(device || '');\n        if (!/^[A-Za-z0-9_./\\-]+$/.test(dev)) { cb(cached); return; }\n        var cmd = [\n            'if pgrep -f \"' + MATCH + '\" >/dev/null; then echo FW_BUSY; exit 0; fi',\n            'stty -F \"' + dev + '\" 115200 raw -echo -icanon -opost -ixon -ixoff min 0 time 30 2>/dev/null',\n            'exec 3<>\"' + dev + '\" || { echo FW_NODEV; exit 0; }',\n            // ver 1, type 3 (hello), seq 1, len 0, CRC-16/CCITT-FALSE of 01 03 01 00 00 = 0xD3D6\n            'printf \"\\\\245\\\\132\\\\001\\\\003\\\\001\\\\000\\\\000\\\\000\\\\326\\\\323\" >&3',\n            'dd bs=32 count=1 <&3 2>/dev/null | tr -d \"\\\\000\\\\015\"'\n        ].join('\\n');\n        var p = run(ctx, cmd, 8000);\n        if (!p) { cb(cached); return; }\n        p.then(function (r) {\n            var text = String((r && r.stdout) || '');\n            var m = /AMBI1\\s+(\\d+)\\s+(RGBW|RGB)/.exec(text);\n            if (!m) {\n                cached.note = /FW_BUSY/.test(text) ? 'service running - using last known board value'\n                                                   : 'board did not answer - using last known value';\n                cb(cached);\n                return;\n            }\n            var live = { leds: Number(m[1]), type: m[2], source: 'firmware' };\n            try { ctx.config.set({ firmwareLeds: live.leds, firmwareType: live.type }); } catch (e) {}\n            cb(live);\n        }, function () { cb(cached); });\n    }\n\n    function saveConfig(values, cb) {\n        readConfigAsync(ctx, function (cfg) {\n            for (var key in values) {\n                if (Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(values, key)) cfg[key] = values[key];\n            }\n            // Same restriction as reads: the Shard cannot write /opt/... itself. Write via the root\n            // helper and rename atomically, so the app never sees a half-written config.json.\n            var json = JSON.stringify(cfg, null, 2) + '\\n';\n            var cmd = 'cat > ' + CONFIG + '.tmp <<\\'AMBCONFIG\\'\\n' + json + 'AMBCONFIG\\n' +\n                      'mv -f ' + CONFIG + '.tmp ' + CONFIG + '\\nchmod 666 ' + CONFIG;\n            var p = run(ctx, cmd, 10000);\n            if (!p) { cb('execute unavailable'); return; }\n            p.then(function () { cb(null); }, function (e) { cb(String(e && e.message || e)); });\n        });\n    }\n\n    function readBody(req, cb) {\n        var chunks = [], size = 0, done = false;\n        req.on('data', function (c) {\n            if (done) return;\n            size += c.length;\n            if (size > 65536) { done = true; cb(null, new Error('body too large')); return; }\n            chunks.push(c);\n        });\n        req.on('end', function () {\n            if (done) return;\n            done = true;\n            try { cb(JSON.parse(Buffer.concat(chunks).toString('utf8'))); }\n            catch (e) { cb(null, e); }\n        });\n    }\n\n    var page = null;\n\n    return {\n        start: function () {\n            page = loadPage();\n            // Boot path. A failing start must not take the Shard down, so the promise is handled\n            // here rather than thrown.\n            act(START, 30000, 'start');\n        },\n\n        stop: function () {\n            page = null;\n        },\n\n        status: function () {\n            return {\n                state: cache.state,\n                pid: cache.pid,\n                device: cache.device,\n                module: cache.module,\n                version: cache.version,\n                lastAction: cache.lastAction,\n                lastError: cache.lastError || undefined\n            };\n        },\n\n        route: function (req, res, sub) {\n            if (sub === 'ui' && req.method === 'GET') {\n                res.writeHead(200, { 'content-type': 'text/html; charset=utf-8', 'cache-control': 'no-store' });\n                res.end(page || loadPage());\n                return true;\n            }\n            if (sub === 'state' && req.method === 'GET') {\n                refresh(function () {\n                    logTail(25, function (log) {\n                        json(res, { state: cache.state, pid: cache.pid, device: cache.device,\n                            module: cache.module, version: cache.version, serial: cache.serial,\n                            captureProblem: cache.captureProblem, lastAction: cache.lastAction,\n                            lastError: cache.lastError, log: log });\n                    });\n                });\n                return true;\n            }\n            if (sub === 'output' && req.method === 'POST') {\n                readBody(req, function (body, err) {\n                    if (err) { json(res, { ok: false, error: err.message }, 400); return; }\n                    var v = Number(body && body.enabled);\n                    if (v !== 0 && v !== 1) {\n                        json(res, { ok: false, errors: ['enabled must be 0 or 1'] }, 400);\n                        return;\n                    }\n                    // Live: the app polls /tmp/amb-control when no controlUrl is configured. The\n                    // SCORPIO blanks the strip ~400 ms after the last frame, so no restart is needed.\n                    var p = run(ctx, 'printf \"enable=' + v + '\\\\n\" > /tmp/amb-control', 5000);\n                    if (!p) { json(res, { ok: false, error: 'execute unavailable' }, 500); return; }\n                    p.then(function () {\n                        // Persist for the next service start as well (config is read only at startup).\n                        saveConfig({ outputEnabled: v }, function (saveErr) {\n                            if (saveErr) { json(res, { ok: false, error: saveErr }, 500); return; }\n                            json(res, { ok: true, enabled: v });\n                        });\n                    }, function (e) { json(res, { ok: false, error: String(e && e.message || e) }, 500); });\n                });\n                return true;\n            }\n            if (sub === 'config' && req.method === 'GET') {\n                readConfigAsync(ctx, function (cfg) {\n                    probeFirmware(function (fw) {\n                        json(res, { config: cfg, firmware: fw, defaults: DEFAULTS, specs: SPECS });\n                    });\n                });\n                return true;\n            }\n            if (sub === 'config' && req.method === 'POST') {\n                readBody(req, function (body, err) {\n                    if (err) { json(res, { ok: false, error: err.message }, 400); return; }\n                    probeFirmware(function (fw) {\n                        var checked = validate(body && body.values, fw.leds);\n                        if (checked.errors.length) { json(res, { ok: false, errors: checked.errors }, 400); return; }\n                        saveConfig(checked.clean, function (saveErr) {\n                            if (saveErr) { json(res, { ok: false, error: saveErr }, 500); return; }\n                            var done = function () {\n                                json(res, { ok: true, values: checked.clean, firmware: fw,\n                                            restarted: !!(body && body.restart) });\n                            };\n                            if (body && body.restart) {\n                                act(STOP, 40000, 'stop', function () {\n                                    act(START, 30000, 'start', done);\n                                });\n                            } else done();\n                        });\n                    });\n                });\n                return true;\n            }\n            if (req.method !== 'POST') return false;\n            if (sub === 'start') { act(START, 30000, 'start', function () { json(res, { ok: true, state: cache.state, lastAction: cache.lastAction }); }); return true; }\n            if (sub === 'stop') { act(STOP, 40000, 'stop', function () { json(res, { ok: true, state: cache.state, lastAction: cache.lastAction }); }); return true; }\n            if (sub === 'restart') {\n                act(STOP, 40000, 'stop', function () {\n                    act(START, 30000, 'start', function () { json(res, { ok: true, state: cache.state, lastAction: cache.lastAction }); });\n                });\n                return true;\n            }\n            return false;\n        }\n    };\n};\n","ui.html":"<!doctype html>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"color-scheme\" content=\"light dark\">\n<title>Ambilight</title>\n<style>\n  :root { font: 15px system-ui, sans-serif; }\n  body { margin: 0; padding: 16px; max-width: 860px; }\n  h1 { font-size: 18px; margin: 0 0 12px; }\n  h2 { font-size: 14px; margin: 18px 0 8px; }\n  #state { font-family: ui-monospace, monospace; padding: 10px 12px; border: 1px solid #8884; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 12px; white-space: pre-wrap; }\n  button { font: inherit; padding: 7px 12px; margin: 0 6px 6px 0; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid #8888; background: #8882; cursor: pointer; }\n  button:disabled { opacity: .5; cursor: default; }\n  button.primary { background: #26a269; color: white; border-color: #26a269; }\n  button.off { background: #8882; color: inherit; border-color: #8888; }\n  fieldset { border: 1px solid #8884; border-radius: 8px; margin: 0 0 12px; padding: 10px 12px 4px; }\n  legend { font-weight: 600; padding: 0 6px; }\n  .grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(215px, 1fr)); gap: 8px 14px; }\n  label { display: block; font-size: 12px; opacity: .85; }\n  input { font: inherit; width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; padding: 5px 6px; border: 1px solid #8886; border-radius: 6px; background: transparent; color: inherit; }\n  .hint { font-size: 11px; opacity: .65; }\n  #fw { font-size: 13px; padding: 8px 10px; background: #8882; border-radius: 8px; }\n  #msg { font-size: 13px; min-height: 18px; margin: 8px 0; color: #c33; white-space: pre-wrap; }\n  pre { font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.35; background: #8881; padding: 10px; border-radius: 8px; overflow: auto; max-height: 35vh; margin: 0; }\n</style>\n<h1>Ambilight</h1>\n<div id=\"state\">loading…</div>\n<div>\n  <button id=\"start\">Start</button>\n  <button id=\"stop\">Stop</button>\n  <button id=\"restart\">Restart</button>\n</div>\n<div>\n  <button id=\"outputToggle\" class=\"primary\">Ambilight: ON</button>\n</div>\n\n<h2>Settings</h2>\n<div id=\"fw\">reading the board…</div>\n<div id=\"msg\"></div>\n<fieldset>\n  <legend>Layout preview — click the ring to place LED 0</legend>\n  <canvas id=\"ring\" width=\"640\" height=\"380\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:640px;cursor:crosshair;border-radius:6px\"></canvas>\n  <div class=\"hint\">Colours run in physical LED order: red → green → blue → red. Grey ticks are zone\n  boundaries. Click or drag anywhere on the perimeter to move the start; the white ring is LED 0.</div>\n  <div>\n    <button id=\"rev\">Flip direction</button>\n    <button id=\"topleft\">Start top-left</button>\n    <button id=\"gap\">Start at bottom gap</button>\n    <button id=\"mycut\">My cut 97/53/97/53</button>\n    <button id=\"vivid\">Vivid colours</button>\n  </div>\n  <div id=\"ringinfo\" class=\"hint\">—</div>\n</fieldset>\n<fieldset>\n  <legend>Geometry — where the light goes</legend>\n  <div class=\"grid\" id=\"geometry\"></div>\n</fieldset>\n<fieldset>\n  <legend>Look &amp; feel — how it reacts</legend>\n  <div class=\"grid\" id=\"look\"></div>\n</fieldset>\n<div>\n  <button id=\"preset\">77″ / 300 LEDs</button>\n  <button id=\"resetgeo\">Reset geometry</button>\n  <button id=\"save\" class=\"primary\">Save</button>\n  <button id=\"saverestart\" class=\"primary\">Save &amp; restart</button>\n</div>\n<p class=\"hint\">Settings are read by the service only at startup. \"Save &amp; restart\" applies them now;\nthe board's compiled LED count is the hard upper limit.</p>\n\n<h2 style=\"font-size:14px;margin:16px 0 8px\">run.log (tail)</h2>\n<pre id=\"log\">…</pre>\n<script>\n(function () {\n  var $ = function (id) { return document.getElementById(id); };\n  var busy = false;\n  var fw = { leds: 300, type: 'RGBW', source: 'cached' };\n  var outputOn = true;\n\n  function renderOutput() {\n    var b = $('outputToggle');\n    b.textContent = 'Ambilight: ' + (outputOn ? 'ON' : 'OFF') + ' — click to turn ' + (outputOn ? 'off' : 'on');\n    b.className = outputOn ? 'primary' : 'off';\n  }\n\n  // Mirrors SPECS in index.js. The board's LED count replaces the fixed maximum at load time.\n  var FIELDS = [\n    { g:'geometry', k:'ledCount',   t:'LEDs on the strip',      min:1,    max:300, step:1,    hint:'must match the firmware (compiled in)' },\n    { g:'geometry', k:'zoneCount',  t:'Zones around the ring',  min:1,    max:300, step:1,    hint:'one zone per LED by default' },\n    { g:'geometry', k:'zoneTop',    t:'Top section LEDs',       min:0,    max:300, step:1,    hint:'0 = proportional; your cut: 97' },\n    { g:'geometry', k:'zoneRight',  t:'Right section LEDs',     min:0,    max:300, step:1,    hint:'0 = proportional; your cut: 53' },\n    { g:'geometry', k:'zoneBottom', t:'Bottom section LEDs',    min:0,    max:300, step:1,    hint:'0 = proportional; your cut: 97' },\n    { g:'geometry', k:'zoneLeft',   t:'Left section LEDs',      min:0,    max:300, step:1,    hint:'0 = proportional; your cut: 53' },\n    { g:'geometry', k:'mapOffset',  t:'Start offset (LED)',     min:0,    max:299, step:1,    hint:'where LED 0 sits (bottom-right start = 149)' },\n    { g:'geometry', k:'mapReverse', t:'Reverse direction',      min:0,    max:1,   step:1,    hint:'0 = clockwise, 1 = anticlockwise' },\n    { g:'geometry', k:'bandFrac',   t:'Edge band fraction',     min:0.01, max:0.5, step:0.01, hint:'height of each perimeter zone band' },\n    { g:'geometry', k:'bars',       t:'Crop letterbox',         min:0,    max:1,   step:1,    hint:'detect black bars at top/bottom' },\n    { g:'geometry', k:'barRows',    t:'Row-based bar detection',min:0,    max:1,   step:1,    hint:'off by default: false positives' },\n    { g:'geometry', k:'barThresh',  t:'Bar threshold',          min:0,    max:255, step:1,    hint:'luma below this counts as a bar' },\n    { g:'look', k:'alpha',      t:'Smoothing (alpha)',      min:0,   max:1,   step:0.01, hint:'lower = smoother, slower' },\n    { g:'look', k:'gamma',      t:'Gamma',                  min:0.5, max:4,   step:0.05, hint:'1 = no lift, matches the captured frame' },\n    { g:'look', k:'adaptiveGamma', t:'Adaptive gamma',      min:0,   max:1,   step:1,    hint:'off: gamma stays at the value above' },\n    { g:'look', k:'saturation', t:'Saturation',              min:0.5, max:1,   step:0.05, hint:'keep at 1; above 1 clips low channels and shifts hue' },\n    { g:'look', k:'black',      t:'Black level',             min:0,   max:200, step:1,    hint:'lifts every channel; lower = deeper colours' },\n    { g:'look', k:'spatial',    t:'Neighbour blur',          min:0,   max:1,   step:0.05, hint:'blends adjacent zones; lower = tighter colours' },\n    { g:'look', k:'peak',       t:'HDR peak (nits)',         min:100, max:4000,step:10,   hint:'assumed HDR highlight level; higher = less pastel' },\n    { g:'look', k:'hdr',        t:'HDR / PQ input',          min:0,   max:1,   step:1,    hint:'0 = SDR (this TV); 1 = real HDR sources only' },\n    { g:'look', k:'gamut',      t:'BT.2020 -> BT.709',       min:0,   max:1,   step:1,    hint:'use with hdr=1; leave 0 for SDR' },\n    { g:'look', k:'targetFps',  t:'Target fps',              min:0,   max:120, step:1,    hint:'0 = uncapped; triples on a still image' },\n    { g:'look', k:'staleMs',    t:'Fade after still (ms)',   min:0,   max:60000, step:500,  hint:'0 = never fade' },\n    { g:'look', k:'staleLevel', t:'Fade to',                 min:0,   max:1,   step:0.05, hint:'brightness while the picture is frozen' },\n    { g:'look', k:'punch',      t:'Scene-change punch',      min:0,   max:1,   step:0.05, hint:'brief boost on a cut' }\n  ];\n\n  // The values this TV is calibrated with. Kept in sync with index.js DEFAULTS and with the\n  // working /opt/usr/share/ambilight/config.json. hdr/gamut=0 matter: the PQ/BT.2020 path shifts\n  // saturated SDR hues (orange -> yellow), so a fresh install must not start with them enabled.\n  var DEFAULTS = {\n    ledCount:300, zoneCount:300, zoneTop:97, zoneRight:53, zoneBottom:97, zoneLeft:53,\n    mapOffset:149, mapReverse:1, bandFrac:0.08,\n    bars:1, barRows:0, barThresh:18, alpha:0.25, gamma:1, saturation:1, adaptiveGamma:0,\n    targetFps:25, staleMs:6000, staleLevel:0.35, punch:0,\n    black:2, spatial:0.15, peak:400, hdr:0, gamut:0\n  };\n\n  function build() {\n    FIELDS.forEach(function (f) {\n      var wrap = document.createElement('div');\n      var lab = document.createElement('label');\n      lab.textContent = f.t;\n      var inp = document.createElement('input');\n      inp.type = 'number'; inp.id = 'f_' + f.k; inp.min = f.min; inp.max = f.max; inp.step = f.step;\n      // Seed with the calibrated defaults NOW. getConfig() below replaces them with the live values,\n      // but if that fetch fails the fields must not be blank and the preview must not fall back to\n      // mapOffset 0 (upper-left) - a blank panel looks like an unset config even when the TV is fine.\n      inp.value = DEFAULTS[f.k];\n      lab.appendChild(inp); wrap.appendChild(lab);\n      var hint = document.createElement('div'); hint.className = 'hint'; hint.textContent = f.hint;\n      wrap.appendChild(hint);\n      $(f.g).appendChild(wrap);\n    });\n  }\n\n  function setValues(vals) {\n    FIELDS.forEach(function (f) {\n      var v = vals[f.k];\n      if (v === undefined || v === null) v = DEFAULTS[f.k];\n      $('f_' + f.k).value = v;\n    });\n  }\n\n  function values() {\n    var out = {};\n    FIELDS.forEach(function (f) { out[f.k] = Number($('f_' + f.k).value); });\n    return out;\n  }\n\n  function msg(text, isError) {\n    $('msg').textContent = text || '';\n    $('msg').style.color = isError ? '#c33' : '#2a7';\n  }\n\n  function setBusy(b) {\n    busy = b;\n    ['start','stop','restart','outputToggle','save','saverestart','preset','resetgeo'].forEach(function (k) { $(k).disabled = b; });\n  }\n\n  function render(s) {\n    var lines = [\n      'state   : ' + (s.state || '?'),\n      'pid     : ' + (s.pid || '-'),\n      'device  : ' + (s.device || '-'),\n      'module  : ' + (s.module || '-'),\n      'version : ' + (s.version || '-'),\n      'serial  : ' + (s.serial || '-')\n    ];\n    if (s.captureProblem) lines.push('capture : ' + s.captureProblem);\n    if (s.lastAction) lines.push('action  : ' + s.lastAction);\n    if (s.lastError) lines.push('error   : ' + s.lastError);\n    $('state').textContent = lines.join('\\n');\n    $('log').textContent = s.log || '(no log yet)';\n  }\n\n  function getState() {\n    return fetch('state', { cache:'no-store' }).then(function (r) { return r.json(); }).then(render);\n  }\n\n  function getConfig() {\n    return fetch('config', { cache:'no-store' }).then(function (r) { return r.json(); }).then(function (d) {\n      fw = d.firmware || fw;\n      if (d.config && d.config.outputEnabled !== undefined) {\n        outputOn = Number(d.config.outputEnabled) !== 0;\n        renderOutput();\n      }\n      $('fw').textContent = 'Board: ' + fw.leds + ' LEDs, ' + fw.type + ' (' + fw.source + ')' +\n        (fw.note ? ' — ' + fw.note : '');\n      if (fw.source === 'firmware') {\n        ['ledCount','zoneCount','mapOffset'].forEach(function (k) {\n          var el = $('f_' + k);\n          if (el) el.max = (k === 'mapOffset') ? fw.leds - 1 : fw.leds;\n        });\n      }\n      setValues(d.config || d.defaults || {});\n      // setValues changes the fields the preview reads; without this the first draw happened with\n      // empty inputs, so the preview showed the proportional split even when an exact cut was saved.\n      ringDraw();\n    });\n  }\n\n  function go(what) {\n    if (busy) return;\n    setBusy(true);\n    $('state').textContent = what + '…';\n    fetch(what, { method:'POST' }).then(function () { return getState(); })\n      .catch(function (e) { msg('error: ' + e); }).then(function () { setBusy(false); });\n  }\n\n  function save(restart) {\n    if (busy) return;\n    setBusy(true); msg('saving…');\n    fetch('config', {\n      method: 'POST', headers: { 'content-type':'application/json' },\n      body: JSON.stringify({ values: values(), restart: restart })\n    }).then(function (r) { return r.json().then(function (d) { return { ok:r.ok, body:d }; }); })\n      .then(function (d) {\n        if (!d.ok || !d.body.ok) {\n          msg((d.body.errors || [d.body.error || 'save failed']).join('\\n'), true);\n        } else {\n          msg('saved' + (restart ? ' and restarted' : '') + '.', false);\n          return getConfig().then(getState);\n        }\n      })\n      .catch(function (e) { msg('error: ' + e, true); })\n      .then(function () { setBusy(false); });\n  }\n\n  $('start').onclick = function () { go('start'); };\n  $('stop').onclick = function () { go('stop'); };\n  $('restart').onclick = function () { go('restart'); };\n  $('outputToggle').onclick = function () {\n    if (busy) return;\n    setBusy(true); msg('switching ambilight…');\n    var want = outputOn ? 0 : 1;\n    fetch('output', {\n      method: 'POST', headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json' },\n      body: JSON.stringify({ enabled: want })\n    }).then(function (r) { return r.json().then(function (d) { return { ok: r.ok, body: d }; }); })\n      .then(function (d) {\n        if (!d.ok || !d.body.ok) { msg((d.body.errors || [d.body.error || 'switch failed']).join('\\n'), true); return; }\n        outputOn = Number(d.body.enabled) !== 0;\n        renderOutput();\n        msg('Ambilight turned ' + (outputOn ? 'on' : 'off') + '.', false);\n      })\n      .catch(function (e) { msg('error: ' + e, true); })\n      .then(function () { setBusy(false); });\n  };\n  $('save').onclick = function () { save(false); };\n  $('saverestart').onclick = function () { save(true); };\n  $('preset').onclick = function () { setValues(DEFAULTS); msg('preset loaded — press Save to apply.', false); };\n  $('resetgeo').onclick = function () {\n    ['mapOffset','mapReverse','bandFrac','bars','barRows','barThresh'].forEach(function (k) {\n      $('f_' + k).value = DEFAULTS[k];\n    });\n    $('f_zoneCount').value = $('f_ledCount').value;\n    msg('geometry reset — press Save to apply.', false);\n  };\n  $('vivid').onclick = function () {\n    // Counter the per-channel gamma lift, the black-level lift and the neighbour blur. Gamma and\n    // saturation stay at 1: >1 on either lifts/clips the captured plane (greens lost all their red).\n    $('f_gamma').value = 1; $('f_saturation').value = 1; $('f_adaptiveGamma').value = 0;\n    $('f_black').value = 2; $('f_spatial').value = 0.15;\n    $('f_punch').value = 0; $('f_peak').value = 400;\n    msg('vivid preset loaded — press Save & restart to apply.', false);\n  };\n\n  // ---- clickable layout preview -------------------------------------------------\n  // Mirrors ZoneLayout in ZoneEngine.cs: zones are distributed over the four edges in proportion to\n  // their length and walked top L->R, right T->B, bottom R->L, left B->T. LED n is fed zone\n  // (n + mapOffset) mod zoneCount, or (-n + mapOffset) when reversed. So the visual order is the real\n  // order the strip receives, not an approximation.\n  var RING = { x: 30, y: 27, w: 580, h: 326.25 };\n  function mod(n, m) { return ((n % m) + m) % m; }\n\n  function ringZones(total) {\n    var W = 960, H = 540, per = 2 * W + 2 * H, i;\n    var et = Number($('f_zoneTop').value) || 0, er = Number($('f_zoneRight').value) || 0,\n        eb = Number($('f_zoneBottom').value) || 0, el = Number($('f_zoneLeft').value) || 0;\n    if (et > 0 && er > 0 && eb > 0 && el > 0) {\n      // Exact cut list from the UI. Surplus slots go at the bottom-centre cut, AFTER the left edge,\n      // exactly as ZoneEngine.cs does, so every real LED keeps its position from the cut list.\n      var sum = et + er + eb + el;\n      while (sum > total && eb > 1) { eb--; sum--; }\n      while (sum > total && (et > 1 || er > 1 || el > 1)) {\n        if (et >= er && et >= el && et > 1) et--;\n        else if (er >= el && er > 1) er--;\n        else el--;\n        sum--;\n      }\n      var spare = total - sum, out = [];\n      for (i = 0; i < et; i++) out.push({ x: (i + 0.5) / et, y: 0 });\n      for (i = 0; i < er; i++) out.push({ x: 1, y: (i + 0.5) / er });\n      // Pitch is set by the TOP section (97 LEDs across the top width), not by the bottom count.\n      // Each bottom section grows inward from its own corner, so a short section leaves a wide\n      // empty middle instead of being stretched across the whole edge.\n      var pitch = 1 / et, halfRight = Math.ceil(eb / 2), halfLeft = eb - halfRight;\n      for (i = 0; i < halfRight; i++) out.push({ x: 1 - (i + 0.5) * pitch, y: 1 });\n      for (i = 0; i < halfLeft; i++) out.push({ x: (halfLeft - i - 0.5) * pitch, y: 1 });\n      for (i = 0; i < el; i++) out.push({ x: 0, y: 1 - (i + 0.5) / el });\n      for (i = 0; i < spare; i++) out.push({ x: 0.5, y: 1 });\n      return { list: out, top: et, right: er, bottom: eb, left: el,\n               spare: spare, total: out.length, explicit: true, gap: pitch };\n    }\n    var left = Math.max(1, Math.round(total * H / per));\n    var top = Math.max(1, Math.round(total * W / per));\n    var right = left, bottom = top;\n    var sum = left + top + right + bottom;\n    while (sum < total) { bottom++; sum++; }\n    while (sum > total && bottom > 1) { bottom--; sum--; }\n    var out = [];\n    for (i = 0; i < top; i++) out.push({ x: (i + 0.5) / top, y: 0 });\n    for (i = 0; i < right; i++) out.push({ x: 1, y: (i + 0.5) / right });\n    for (i = 0; i < bottom; i++) out.push({ x: 1 - (i + 0.5) / bottom, y: 1 });\n    for (i = 0; i < left; i++) out.push({ x: 0, y: 1 - (i + 0.5) / left });\n    return { list: out, top: top, right: right, bottom: bottom, left: left,\n             spare: 0, total: out.length, explicit: false };\n  }\n\n  function ringPos(p) { return { x: RING.x + p.x * RING.w, y: RING.y + p.y * RING.h }; }\n\n  function ringSettings() {\n    return {\n      z: ringZones(Math.max(1, Number($('f_zoneCount').value) || 300)),\n      leds: Math.max(1, Number($('f_ledCount').value) || 300),\n      offset: Math.max(0, Number($('f_mapOffset').value) || 0),\n      reverse: Number($('f_mapReverse').value) === 1\n    };\n  }\n\n  function ringDraw() {\n    var s = ringSettings(), c = $('ring'), g = c.getContext('2d'), led;\n    g.clearRect(0, 0, c.width, c.height);\n    g.fillStyle = '#8881'; g.fillRect(RING.x, RING.y, RING.w, RING.h);\n    g.strokeStyle = '#8887'; g.lineWidth = 2; g.strokeRect(RING.x, RING.y, RING.w, RING.h);\n    // The physical cut in the strip (bottom centre) is not a software zone; draw it so the\n    // \"Start at bottom gap\" button has a visible target.\n    var gx = RING.x + RING.w / 2, gy = RING.y + RING.h;\n    g.strokeStyle = '#fff'; g.lineWidth = 2; g.setLineDash([3, 3]);\n    g.beginPath(); g.moveTo(gx, gy - 11); g.lineTo(gx, gy + 11); g.stroke();\n    g.setLineDash([]);\n    g.font = '12px system-ui'; g.fillStyle = '#aaa'; g.textAlign = 'center';\n    g.fillText('gap', gx, gy + 26); g.textAlign = 'start';\n    g.fillStyle = '#8886';\n    s.z.list.forEach(function (p) { var q = ringPos(p); g.beginPath(); g.arc(q.x, q.y, 2, 0, 6.283); g.fill(); });\n    for (led = 0; led < s.leds; led++) {\n      var zi = mod((s.reverse ? -led : led) + s.offset, s.z.total);\n      if (zi >= s.z.total - s.z.spare) continue;   // the cut: nothing is physically there\n      var q = ringPos(s.z.list[zi]);\n      g.fillStyle = 'hsl(' + Math.round(360 * led / s.leds) + ',85%,55%)';\n      g.beginPath(); g.arc(q.x, q.y, 3.2, 0, 6.283); g.fill();\n      if (led === 0) {\n        g.strokeStyle = '#fff'; g.lineWidth = 2;\n        g.beginPath(); g.arc(q.x, q.y, 7, 0, 6.283); g.stroke();\n      }\n    }\n    if (s.z.explicit) {\n      g.font = '12px system-ui'; g.fillStyle = '#aaa'; g.textAlign = 'center';\n      g.fillText(String(s.z.top), RING.x + RING.w / 2, RING.y - 8);\n      g.fillText(String(s.z.right), RING.x + RING.w + 16, RING.y + RING.h / 2);\n      g.fillText(String(s.z.bottom), RING.x + RING.w / 2, RING.y + RING.h - 10);\n      g.fillText(String(s.z.left), RING.x - 16, RING.y + RING.h / 2);\n      g.textAlign = 'start';\n    }\n    $('ringinfo').textContent = 'LED 0 → zone ' + s.offset + ' · ' +\n      (s.reverse ? 'anticlockwise' : 'clockwise') + ' · ' + s.z.total + ' zones (top ' +\n      s.z.top + ', right ' + s.z.right + ', bottom ' + s.z.bottom + ', left ' + s.z.left +\n      (s.z.spare ? ', +' + s.z.spare + ' at the cut' : '') + ')' + (s.z.explicit ? ' — exact cut list' : '');\n  }\n\n  function ringNearest(e) {\n    var c = $('ring'), r = c.getBoundingClientRect();\n    var x = (e.clientX - r.left) * c.width / r.width;\n    var y = (e.clientY - r.top) * c.height / r.height;\n    var z = ringZones(Math.max(1, Number($('f_zoneCount').value) || 300));\n    var best = -1, bd = 1e9;\n    z.list.forEach(function (p, i) {\n      var q = ringPos(p), d = (q.x - x) * (q.x - x) + (q.y - y) * (q.y - y);\n      if (d < bd) { bd = d; best = i; }\n    });\n    return best;\n  }\n\n  function ringSet(e) {\n    var i = ringNearest(e);\n    if (i < 0) return;\n    $('f_mapOffset').value = i;\n    ringDraw();\n  }\n\n  function wireRing() {\n    ['f_ledCount','f_zoneCount','f_mapOffset','f_mapReverse'].forEach(function (k) {\n      $(k).addEventListener('input', ringDraw);\n    });\n    $('ring').addEventListener('click', ringSet);\n    $('rev').onclick = function () {\n      $('f_mapReverse').value = Number($('f_mapReverse').value) === 1 ? 0 : 1;\n      ringDraw();\n    };\n    $('topleft').onclick = function () { $('f_mapOffset').value = 0; ringDraw(); };\n    $('mycut').onclick = function () {\n      // 300 physical LEDs, no gap: top 97, right 53, bottom 97, left 53. The strip starts at the\n      // bottom-right corner and runs counter-clockwise, so LED 0 is zone 149 (mapOffset + reverse).\n      $('f_zoneTop').value = 97; $('f_zoneRight').value = 53;\n      $('f_zoneBottom').value = 97; $('f_zoneLeft').value = 53;\n      $('f_zoneCount').value = 300; $('f_ledCount').value = 300;\n      $('f_mapOffset').value = 149; $('f_mapReverse').value = 1;\n      ringDraw();\n    };\n    $('gap').onclick = function () {\n      // The bottom edge is walked right->left, so its midpoint zone is top + right + bottom/2.\n      // (Forgetting the top count puts the start on the right edge instead - fixed after a report.)\n      var z = ringZones(Math.max(1, Number($('f_zoneCount').value) || 300));\n      $('f_mapOffset').value = z.top + z.right + Math.floor(z.bottom / 2);\n      ringDraw();\n    };\n  }\n\n  build();\n  wireRing();\n  ringDraw();\n  getState();\n  getConfig().catch(function (e) { msg('could not read settings: ' + e, true); });\n  setInterval(getState, 5000);\n})();\n</script>\n"}}